  "metadata": {
    "name": "varcoeff_laplacian_neumann_bc_ast_fixture",
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_laplacian_neumann_bc: a minimal consuming model binding N=8 at the import edge. The compound match D( k * D(u,x), x ) must fire through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint (priority 10) and lower to the rule's makearray -- interior [2,7] holding the imported conservative flux-difference stencil aggregate over u and k, faces i=1 and i=8 holding the prescribed-flux one-sided faces (the dropped-flux zero-flux face value minus qL/dx at i=1, plus qR/dx at i=8) -- with zero apply_expression_template nodes, zero surviving spatial D, and the free names dx, qL, qR surviving in the expanded body. The model declares qL and qR as ordinary real parameters; qL keeps its zero default (homogeneous left wall, so at i=1 the qL/dx term is present but zero) and qR is a nonzero fixed flux, so the golden pins both the homogeneous and the inhomogeneous face spellings. The coefficient k is a consumer-supplied field of shape [x] (here k=1+0.5 cos(2 pi x_i)), bound by the match as the LEFT factor of the product; u is the state. x0 = 0 and dx = 1/8; the dx expression is spelled with the literal 8 because the edge binding closes N before it reaches this document's scope (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm). The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST across bindings.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "ast",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "rule:varcoeff_laplacian_neumann_bc"
    ]
  },
